{"name":"Tarragon","hex":"#a4ae77","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tarragon","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial herb, the wormwood species Artemisia dracunculus, from Europe and parts of Asia.","The leaves of this plant (either fresh, or preserved in a vinegar/oil mixture) used as a seasoning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tarragon"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tarragon","blocks":[{"text":"Tarragon, also known as estragon, is a species of perennial herb in the family Asteraceae. It is widespread in the wild across much of Eurasia and North America and is cultivated for culinary and medicinal purposes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Estragon_1511.jpg/330px-Estragon_1511.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tarragon"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Dried_Taragon.JPG/500px-Dried_Taragon.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Dried_Taragon.JPG/1280px-Dried_Taragon.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c1/Dried_Taragon.JPG/500px-Dried_Taragon.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Dried tarragon leaves","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADried_Taragon.JPG"}],"sounds":{"tarragon":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a5/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-tarragon.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/a5/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-tarragon.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-tarragon.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimed